WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talk a lot about
your family in previous show,

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:06.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your mom actually hid
some of your history from you.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that true?
-Yeah, you know.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, our history,
Latin people,

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were there during
the American Revolution,

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.280
the Civil War, and it´s not in
textbooks, movies or anything.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.484
And my mom was kind of like
that with my father´s history

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.285
because he abandoned our asses.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.888 size:81% position:41%
Pardon me. Excuse me,
but I had to go there.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Excuse him, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You´re allowed
to say that, yeah.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How much do you charge
for 45 minutes.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot less than my real
therapist charges,

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s for sure.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you match your therapist
couch when you go there?

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.938
Do you like where the...?

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have always had a problem
blending in.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:45.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Urban camo.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
Talk show camo.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So she hid stuff
about your --

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.253
-With my dad, she would be like,
"John, I never wanted

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.754
to bad mouth your father.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, because then it would
ruin the moment

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you figured it out
by yourself."

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gotta love that woman.
-That´s very nice.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.563 size:84% position:42%
You have an aversion...

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell me about a Thanksgiving
with your family.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
What´s that like?

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
everybody´s always

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.170
talking over each other,
like three conversations,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
three threads and everybody´s
following it.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a hard time
with Thanksgiving,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I feel like a traitor
when I sit down

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.546
because ever since I was a
little boy, man, I always wished

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.082
there had been some wizened
woman who said to her people

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
before the pilgrims sat down,
"Don´t feed them!

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you feed them,
they´ll never leave!"

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that food
must have been that good,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
not like my mom´s cooking.
-Not good?

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The pilgrims
would have swam back

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
without the goddamn <i>Mayflower,
seriously.</i>

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.701 size:84% position:42%
My mom´s been serving
leftovers for 50 years.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.637
To this day, no one´s ever found
the original meal.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seriously,
I´m not making this up.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um...

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.447
Over the course of you career,
actors obviously have to make

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of choices.
-Yeah.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.217 size:75% position:38%
-Some great. Some...

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not so great.
-I did not realize...

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.155
I knew you had been in the
"Super Mario Bros." movie.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Shh.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.959 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m proud of it.
I´m proud of it now.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.895
-Was it With Bob Hoskins?

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.830 size:88% position:44%
-Yes, and Dennis Hopper.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Dennis Hopper.
-The late Dennis Hopper.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
My acting, I think,
got rid of them, too.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.070
-Oh, no. I don´t think so.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
But those are two guys, of
course you would do that movie

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.274
But you turned down a role
in the film "Philadelphia"...

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes.
-to do "Super Mario Bros."

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was supposed to be
Tom Hanks´ lover,

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I didn´t think he was good
looking enough for me.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Okay.
-I wanted, like Kevin Costner

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.184 size:78% position:39%
or Denzel Washington.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I turned it down
for "Super Mario Bros.",

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.621 size:75% position:38%
and then, of course,
they all won Oscars

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:38.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I won a the "John,
how can you be stupid award?"

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
for my wife.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.662 size:88% position:44%
"Mario Bros." didn´t win
any Oscars. Nominated?

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, not so much.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.734
Maybe a Raspberry.
-I think they´ll make up for it.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it will eventually be
a recognized film.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.438
-Right, as the first video game
ever made into a movie.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.908
-Right. Now, those things
come out once a month.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you were a trail blazer.
-I was a pioneer.

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:58.511
-Thanks so much for being here.

